# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Research data and run artifacts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Speech corpora are never committed — download them and build the local bank
# per each paper's README. AudioMNIST is redistributable but large, and other
# corpora carry their own licences. Each src/data/ carries its own .gitignore
# that keeps only its README, so the directory stays documented but empty.
**/data/AudioMNIST/
**/data/LibriTTS/
**/data/LJSpeech*/
**/data/VCTK*/
**/data/musan/
*.wav.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tar.bz2

# Derived stimulus banks and any other local cache (deterministic, rebuildable
# from the corpus by a committed script).
**/cache/
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt
*.safetensors
*.npz

# Model checkpoints and per-run scratch. Only the per-cell results.json (and
# the trained-arm training curves) are committed under papers/*/results/.
checkpoints/
**/checkpoints/
runs/
**/results/.artifacts/
**/*-instr.pt

# Audio and figures generated INTO a working tree rather than into the
# committed resources/ trees stay local.
scratch/
out/
tmp/

# The built formats now sit beside each manuscript under papers/, and ARE
# committed: a reader who lands on a paper's folder should find the PDF next to
# the Markdown, not a build instruction. (Once CI publishes them as versioned
# release artifacts they come back out of the tree — see the tracking issue.)
# Only the preprocessing scratch is derived-and-disposable.
publishing/.work/

# The arXiv bundles are the exception, caught by the *.tar.gz rule above and
# left there deliberately. They are a submission artifact rather than something
# to read, and tar records an mtime, so the file changes on every build even
# when nothing in the paper did — the one built format that would churn the
# history for no reason. Rebuild one when you need it:
#     FORMATS=arxiv bash publishing/publish.sh 01

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Personal publishing strategy: named contacts, fee-waiver positions, venue
# tactics, and the alumni-affiliation details. This repository is public and
# none of that belongs in it. Kept in the working tree because it is the thing
# actually being worked from.
independent-researcher-publishing-playbook.md
